/** @page api_extensions Camera extension interfaces (internal, uninstalled)

These are **internal, uninstalled extension interfaces**. They are for authors
working with the provider source tree, not for installed MEL consumers. Follow
@ref md_docs_2camera-profile-tutorial "Create a Camera Profile" from admission
to qualification, then compare the @ref md_docs_2camera-profile-examples
"Camera Profile Examples" (reference implementations with source browsers).
See the @ref md_docs_2camera-profile-authoring "camera-profile authoring contract" and
@ref md_docs_2backend-authoring "backend authoring guide" for ownership and
qualification requirements.

@section extension_profile Profile lifecycle and feature services

Register factories and select a binding without camera I/O. On explicit device
open, the adapter invokes @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfile::open
on its chosen @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfile. The returned
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfileState owns admission facts and
capabilities. It applies and reads back configuration, checks preflight before
acquisition, and admits frames using the frozen run settings. State can retire
independently of its parent profile; the backend still owns native acquisition
and leases, and the provider owns MEL publication.

Use @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfileState::configuration for
fresh readback, @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfileState::apply for
ordered writes, and @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfileState::preflight
to check whether the device is ready for a run. See the shared
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::mono_free_running::apply_configuration for a
concrete implementation of partial failure and no rollback.
@ref gige_mel::backend::device_features::IDeviceFeatures is borrowed and
serialized by the adapter; policy must not retain it or SDK handles. Compare
@ref gige_mel::backend::device_features::IDeviceFeatures::read_integer_feature
with @ref gige_mel::backend::device_features::IDeviceFeatures::write_integer
because native constraints can change between planning and each setter.

For acquisition, @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::plan_pool checks capacity
separately from @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ICameraProfileState::validate_frame,
which admits @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::NativeFrameFacts with a checked
source span. Neither a pool size nor a retained owner proves arbitrary pointer
provenance. See @ref src/profiles/frame_policy.hpp "frame facts and layout source".

@subsection extension_monochrome Reusing the default monochrome policy

@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfile and
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfileState implement the
untriggered Continuous, manual-exposure Mono8 and unpacked little-endian Mono12
assumptions. For a derived model, override
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfile::open to construct the
derived state. The @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfileState::MonoFreeRunningProfileState
constructor owns the native snapshot separately from the advertised capabilities.
The inherited @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfileState::configuration
therefore reports actual representable values, not clamped policy values. Add
request checks before delegating to
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfileState::apply, or use
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::MonoFreeRunningProfileState::native_admission
with the snapshot helper when the order of preflight checks differs. See the
Cognex walkthrough in @ref md_docs_2camera-profile-tutorial "Create a Camera Profile".
Composition and independent implementations remain supported. None of these
defaults implements optional interfaces or replaces common MEL channel mechanics.

@section extension_modules Module loading and selection

@ref gige_mel::selection::BackendCatalog owns the factories. Use
@ref gige_mel::selection::BackendCatalog::register_backend(std::string,std::vector<std::string>,gige_mel::selection::BackendCatalog::ProfileBackendConstructor) "gige_mel::selection::BackendCatalog::register_backend"
to declare compatibility and @ref gige_mel::selection::BackendCatalog::create
to construct the exact pair. @ref gige_mel::selection::select_session binds a
specific device ID without inspecting it. None of these operations certify a
camera model or grant control authority.

Use @ref gige_mel::selection::load_profile_module only for a trusted library at
an explicit path; validation is not a sandbox. @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::module::Descriptor
and @ref gige_mel::selection::LoadedProfile describe validation, creation and
lifetime pins. Discovery uses C linkage, but virtual objects, STL types and
shared ownership cross a matched-C++ boundary. Versions and build identity do
not prove toolchain/ABI parity or hardware compatibility. The existing identity
hashes header bytes (including the default bases and native snapshot layout),
so even comment-only edits in that closure require a host
and module rebuild from matching inputs. See
@ref md_docs_2runtime-selection "runtime selection and explicit module loading".

@subsection extension_image_fov Optional profile Image field of view

@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::IProfileImageFieldOfView interprets the complete
actual configuration against an immutable deployment model. Device composition
can use @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::retain_image_field_of_view to forward
through the selected state, including an independently pinned module state.
The operation is bounded, synchronous, and non-reentrant, with no feature I/O.
The common provider validates and freezes the owned radians before acquisition.
The module loader preserves FOV and navigation independently; neither companion
changes base vtables or the descriptor. See
@ref md_docs_2camera-profile-examples "the inherited virtual-optics example".

@section extension_registers Register and transport boundaries

An explicitly opened adapter may expose @ref gige_mel::backend::device_registers::IRegisterDevice.
@ref gige_mel::backend::device_registers::IRegisterDevice::with_registers lends
an @ref gige_mel::backend::device_registers::IDeviceRegisters under the device
operation lock. @ref gige_mel::backend::device_registers::IDeviceRegisters::write_memory
can change device state outside GenApi policy. This 4096-byte native SDK
service is not part of profile module v1, does not bound in-flight SDK calls,
and does not guarantee the number of SDK or wire transactions.

The separate 508-byte @ref gige_mel::controlled_gvcp::IControlledRegisters
experiment's @ref gige_mel::controlled_gvcp::Client uses
@ref gige_mel::controlled_gvcp::Client::create for an explicit loopback endpoint.
The fixture-only @ref gige_mel::controlled_gvcp::ControlOwner
adds explicit @ref gige_mel::controlled_gvcp::ControlOwner::acquire and
@ref gige_mel::controlled_gvcp::ControlOwner::shutdown. Neither is a production
acquisition transport; SDK coexistence and cross-session stale ACK fencing are
unqualified. See @ref md_docs_2device-register-transport "device register/memory access" and
@ref md_docs_2backend-transport-experiments "transport experiments and original validation records".

@subsection extension_navigation Optional profile navigation handler

@verbatim
MEL ImageChannel::send(NavigationReport)
    ↓
Common MEL validation (unchanged)
    ↓
Optional INavigationSink (only when the profile provides a handler)
    ↓
ProfileNavigationBridge
    ↓
IProfileNavigationHandler::prepare_navigation → owned NavigationOperation
    ↓
Backend-owned INavigationOperationPort (SDK-free recording fixture only)
    ↓
Future: qualified transport, detector-defined staging and acceptance
@endverbatim

A profile state may also implement the optional
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::IProfileNavigationHandler. Discover it with
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::navigation_handler; absence means no navigation
processing. Base profile vtables and the module descriptor are unchanged.
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::IProfileNavigationHandler::prepare_navigation
applies sensor policy without device I/O and returns an owned
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::NavigationOperation value with a
profile-defined format, the unchanged complete report and profile-defined bytes.

A backend builds @ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ProfileNavigationBridge with
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ProfileNavigationBridge::create over its own
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::INavigationOperationPort, and delegates
@ref gige_mel::backend::INavigationSink to
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ProfileNavigationBridge::submit.
@ref gige_mel::backend::profiles::ProfileNavigationBridge::shutdown drains before
retirement. Preparation errors are definite; uncertain or control-lost outcomes
map to `timeout` and are never retried. Module wrappers preserve the capability,
and the header is part of the build identity.

Only an SDK-free recording port exercises this path. No production adapter,
authority grant, register write, GVCP transfer or detector protocol is connected.
Transport ACKs, detector processing, navigation-to-image correlation and transfer
alignment remain unqualified; keep vendor addresses out of the common provider
components in `src/provider/` and `src/provider.cpp`.
See @ref md_docs_2camera-profile-authoring "camera-profile authoring",
@ref md_docs_2navigation-backend-forwarding "navigation forwarding" and
@ref md_docs_2qualification-evidence "qualification evidence".
*/
